meta {
  name: Track visit
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/visits/track
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "path": "/gallery/escena-urbana-guatemala",
    "deviceType": "Desktop",
    "referrer": "https://example.com/"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  # Track visit

  `POST /api/visits/track`

  Insert one website visit per call, without deduplication.

  ## Authentication

  Public.

  ## Parameters

  No path or query parameters.

  ## Request body

  | Field | Type | Rules / default |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | path | string or null | / if omitted/null; stored lowercase. |
  | deviceType | string or null | Unknown if blank/null; no validated enum or detection. |
  | referrer | string or null | Optional; stored as supplied. |

  Send Content-Type: application/json.

  ```json
  {
    "path": "/gallery/escena-urbana-guatemala",
    "deviceType": "Desktop",
    "referrer": "https://example.com/"
  }
  ```

  ## Response

  HTTP **200**.

  Empty response body.

  ## Errors

  - 400: malformed JSON or model validation.

  Automatic model validation can return ValidationProblemDetails; explicit controller errors use a message field. Authentication middleware errors may have no body.

  ## Notes

  Returns 200 with no response body. Uses forwarding/proxy headers for IP and geography, User-Agent for the agent, and SHA-256 of IP_agent as userHash. No HTTP endpoint exposes visit statistics.

  Examples contain fictitious data. The assertion checks the successful scenario; a missing record or insufficient permissions can produce a different documented status.
}
